  "body": "`crates/ui/tests/gpu_render.rs::docs_images_match_the_rendered_steps` (from #525, merged as d8cb5a26) fails on Linux at current main (4865500d and later):\n\n```\ndocs pictures drifted from the rendered steps (regenerate with UPDATE_DOCS_IMAGES=1 cargo test -p camcraft-ui --test gpu_render):\nfirst-part-0-blank.png: 6245 pixels differ\nfirst-part-1-face1.png: 6580 pixels differ\nfirst-part-2-2d-pocket1.png: 6913 pixels differ\nfirst-part-3-drill1.png: 6917 pixels differ\n```\n\nIt reproduces on a clean main checkout, so it isn't from any open PR. It also turns every PR's ui suite red, on any PR that runs `gpu_render`.\n\n**Likely cause:** these are pixel goldens rendered on one OS/GPU (the committed PNGs), compared on another (a Linux software adapter), so pixels drift. That's exactly why AGENTS.md \"Pixel snapshots are release-lane\" (#255) keeps PNG goldens `#[ignore]`d out of quick and batch. This one runs in the default suite.\n\n**Fix (pick one):**\n- `#[ignore]` it into the release-tier ui snapshot lane, with the lane named in the reason, like the kittest snapshots; or\n- compare with a tolerance that holds across adapters.\n\nDone means: the default ui suite is green on Linux at main; the docs-image check still runs in the release lane.\n",
